age tab.<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>After sometime, a table will show up in the tab with the resources it analyzed, and how much code is used in the webpage. All the files linked in the webpage (css, js) will be listed in the Coverage tab. Clicking on any resource there will open that resource in the Sources panel with a breakdown of Total Bytes and Unused Bytes.<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>With this breakdown, we can see how many unused bytes are in our CSS files, so we can manually remove them.<\\/p>\"},\"unminified-css\":{\"title\":\"Minify CSS\",\"description\":\"Minifying CSS files can reduce network payload sizes. [Learn how to minify CSS](https:\\/\\/developer.chrome.com\\/docs\\/lighthouse\\/performance\\/unminified-css\\/).\",\"score\":1,\"displayValue\":\"Potential savings of 4\\u00a0KiB\",\"details\":[{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/nparksf.cluster027.hosting.ovh.net\\/wp-content\\/plugins\\/gutenverse\\/assets\\/gtnicon\\/gtnicon.css?ver=1.8.9\",\"wastedPercent\":18.71335783829361,\"wastedBytes\":4158,\"totalBytes\":22220}],\"type\":[\"FCP\",\"LCP\"],\"instructions\":\"<p>On the <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/nparksf.cluster027.hosting.ovh.net\\/wp-admin\\/admin.php?page=w3tc_minify#css\\\">Minifier<\\/a> tab all of the recommended settings are preset. Use the help button to simplify discovery of your CSS and JS files and groups. Pay close attention to the method and location of your JS group embeddings. See the plugin&#039;s <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/api.w3-edge.com\\/v1\\/redirects\\/faq\\/usage\\\">FAQ<\\/a> for more information on usage.<\\/p>\"},\"unminified-javascript\":{\"title\":\"Minify JavaScript\",\"description\":\"Minifying JavaScript files can reduce payload sizes and script parse time. [Learn how to minify JavaScript](https:\\/\\/developer.chrome.com\\/docs\\/lighthouse\\/performance\\/unminified-javascript\\/).\",\"score\":1,\"displayValue\":null,\"details\":[],\"type\":[\"FCP\",\"LCP\"],\"instructions\":\"<p>O