ring smaller JS payloads helps with this. [Learn how to minimize main-thread work](https:\\/\\/developer.chrome.com\\/docs\\/lighthouse\\/performance\\/mainthread-work-breakdown\\/)\",\"score\":0.1,\"displayValue\":\"7.9\\u00a0s\",\"details\":[{\"duration\":4767.343999999982,\"groupLabel\":\"Script Evaluation\",\"group\":\"scriptEvaluation\"},{\"groupLabel\":\"Other\",\"duration\":1319.6399999999924,\"group\":\"other\"},{\"groupLabel\":\"Style & Layout\",\"group\":\"styleLayout\",\"duration\":854.6039999999999},{\"duration\":411.252,\"groupLabel\":\"Garbage Collection\",\"group\":\"garbageCollection\"},{\"group\":\"scriptParseCompile\",\"groupLabel\":\"Script Parsing & Compilation\",\"duration\":260.7799999999999},{\"groupLabel\":\"Rendering\",\"duration\":156.76400000000055,\"group\":\"paintCompositeRender\"},{\"groupLabel\":\"Parse HTML & CSS\",\"duration\":141.7360000000001,\"group\":\"parseHTML\"}],\"type\":[\"TBT\"],\"instructions\":\"<p>Optimizing third-party JavaScript<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>Review your website&#039;s third-party code and remove the ones\\tthat aren&#039;t adding any value to your website.<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p><a target=\\\"_blank\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/web.dev\\/debounce-your-input-handlers\\/\\\">Debouncing your input handlers<\\/a><\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>Avoid using long-running input handlers (which may block scrolling) and do not make style changes in input handlers (which is likely to cause repainting of pixels).<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>Debouncing your input handlers helps solve both of the above problems.<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>Delay 3rd-party JS<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>Reducing JavaScript execution time<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>Reduce your JavaScript payload by implementing code splitting, minifying and compressing your JavaScript code, removing unused code, and following the PRPL pattern. (Use W3 Total Cache Minify for <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/nparksf.cluster027.hosting.ovh.net\\/wp-admin\\/admin.php?page=w3tc_minify#js\\\" alt=\\\"Minify JS\\\">JS<\\/a> and compression.) Use <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/nparksf.cluster027.hosting.ovh.net\\/wp-admin\\/admin.php?page=w3tc_general#cdn\\\" alt=\\\"CDN\\\">CDN<\\/a> and HTTP2 Push if available on server.<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>Reducing CSS parsing time<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>Reduce the time spent parsing CSS by minifying, or deferring non-critical CSS, or removing unused CSS. (Use W3 Total Cache Minify for <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/nparksf.cluster027.hosting.ovh.net\\/wp-admin\\/admin.php?page=w3tc_minify#css\\\" alt=\\\"Minify CSS\\\">CSS<\\/a> and compression.) Use <a target=\\\"_blank\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/nparksf.cluster027.hosting.ovh.net\\/wp-admin\\/admin.php?page=w3tc_general#cdn\\\" alt=\\\"CDN\\\">CDN<\\/a> and HTTP2 Push if available on server.<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p><a target=\\\"_blank\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/developers.google.com\\/web\\/fundamentals\\/performance\\/rendering\\/stick-to-compositor-only-properties-and-manage-layer-count\\\">Only using compositor properties<\\/a><\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>Stick to using compositor properties to keep events away from the main-thread. Compositor properties are run on a separate compositor thread, freeing the main-thread for longer and improving your page load performance.<\\/p>\"},\"third-party-summary\":{\"title\":\"Reduce the impact of third-party code\",\"description\":\"Third-party code can significantly impact load performance. Limit the number of redundant third-party providers and try to load third-party code after your page has primarily finished loading. [Learn how to minimize third-party impact](https:\\/\\/developers.google.com\\/web\\/fundamentals\\/performance\\/optimizing-content-efficiency\\/loading-third-party-javascript\\/).\",\"score\":0,\"displayValue\":\"Third-party code blocked the main thread for 1,400\\u00a0ms\",\"details\":[{\"transferSize\":